Eric LUTHERER (eric@cimosa.grenoble.hp.com) wrote:

> We are planning to use Oracle 7 database in conjunction with the DCE product
> from OSF on HP platforms. We wonder at which level Oracle 7 and DCE can
> interoperate together, especially when using DCE multi-threading capabilities.

> Which kind of precautionary measures do we need to take when using Oracle 7 
> access in different threads of the same UNIX process ?

   I think you are going to have to make some interesting *design* decisions.
For example, Oracle (or any toher RDBMS for that matter) offers its own
security and naming services, and of course so does DCE.  So you are
going to be constantly choosing between two distinct ways of accomplishing
the same type of thing.


    Also, I am curious about how you plan to implement two- or three-
tiered systems using Oracle 7.  

    From what I can see (I haven't tried any of this, but I have thought
about it a little) you can (1) use all of Oracle's many capabilities,
and then have a hard time fitting it and DCE together, or (2) you can
use Oracle as a sort of dumb database backend, and lose may of Oracle's
useful capabilities.

    Tough choice.


