In article <C9p0zp.D8x@hpwin052.uksr.hp.com>, eric@cimosa.grenoble.hp.com (Eric LUTHERER) writes:
>
> We are planning to use Oracle 7 database in conjunction with the DCE product
> from OSF on HP platforms. We wonder at which level Oracle 7 and DCE can
> interoperate together, especially when using DCE multi-threading capabilities.
>
> Which kind of precautionary measures do we need to take when using Oracle 7
> access in different threads of the same UNIX process ?
>
That depends on the implementation of the DCE-port on HP platforms. There may
be problems because if you have a connection with pipes out of threads to
ORACLE this may not work !
DCE-Pipe I/O is normally implemented NON-BLOCKING. If you don't have a
ORACLE engine prepared for DCE, you'll get an error message because ORACLE
relies on BLOCKING pipe-I/O.

So my advice is:  Try a prototype somewhere first, because it may not work !!

Norbert
